      "what": "This study introduces a directional Latent Demand Index that uses a pooled Poisson regression framework on large-scale, anonymized mobility traces to identify unmet travel needs. By combining this index with a schedule-based Transit Service Index derived from GTFS data, the framework maps directional service gaps at the link level. Applying the method to Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania, revealed that 43.7% of high-demand directed edges receive below-median transit service, with these mismatches concentrated in specific, asymmetric corridors.",
